      en: "The Hanko Front Museum in Finland documents the battles of the Hanko Front during World War II. Hanko was a Soviet-leased territory, recaptured by Finnish forces in 1941. The museum is housed in a former military barracks. It displays weapons, uniforms, and photographs from the period, as well as civilian items. The museum offers guided tours and educational programs. It commemorates the harsh conditions endured by soldiers. The Hanko Peninsula itself contains numerous bunkers and fortifications from the war.",
