      en: "The Finlayson industrial area in Tampere is a historic textile factory complex founded in 1820 by the Scotsman James Finlayson. It was Finland's first large-scale industrial facility and significantly contributed to Tampere's development as an industrial city. The complex comprises several red brick buildings, including the spinning mill, weaving mill, and boiler house. The most distinctive structure is the Finlayson Palace, built in 1844. The area was converted in the 1990s into a cultural and business center, featuring museums, shops, restaurants, and the Tampere Art Museum. The landmark of the complex is the tall chimney, erected in 1866.",
